jobs.description:
Are you a hands-on worker, do you like working in an organized way, and do you feel at home in a logistics environment? Would you like to be part of one of Europe’s largest producers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position at our client in Waalwijk is perfect for you!

As a Logistics Employee, you play an important role in the logistics process surrounding the production of high-quality, custom-made sandwich panels for, among others, the bodywork industry and the defense sector. You ensure that materials, raw materials, and finished products are available at the right place and at the right time.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, in a close-knit team of colleagues. Order, overview, and safety are central to your daily tasks.

As a Logistics Employee, your tasks include:

- Loading and unloading goods using a forklift;

- Receiving and assisting drivers (first point of contact);

- Packing and preparing finished products for shipment;

- Managing internal logistics between the warehouse and production departments;

- Supplying raw materials to various production departments;

- Cleaning and organizing the warehouse and production halls;

- Ensuring a safe and tidy workplace.

Requirements

- You work in a structured manner and have an eye for order and safety;

- You hold a valid forklift certificate;

- You are a true team player;

- You have a good command of the Dutch or English language.

Are you well-organised, communicative, and do you enjoy working with drivers, applicants and colleagues on a daily basis? For a transport company, we are looking for a Planning, Recruitment & HR Coordinator.
 This is a varied position combining transport planning, recruitment and HR responsibilities.
 What will you be doing? You will be an important link between the planning department, drivers, applicants and the organisation. You will support the daily transport planning while also being involved in the recruitment and support of employees.
 Your responsibilities will include:
  - Supporting the daily transport planning;
 - Coordinating and supporting drivers;
 - Communicating with drivers about schedules, changes and any issues that may arise;
 - Responding quickly to changes or problems during the day;
 - Contacting new applicants by phone;
 - Conducting initial telephone interviews with candidates;
 - Scheduling and following up on job interviews;
 - Starting and monitoring the recruitment process;
 - Contributing ideas for the recruitment and selection of new drivers and employees;
 - Actively contributing to HR and personnel policies;
 - Keeping personnel files complete and up to date;
 - Checking whether required documents, information and certificates are complete and valid;
 - Identifying missing documents or documents that are about to expire;
 - Supporting other administrative and organisational tasks related to employees and planning.

 Who are we looking for? We are looking for someone who communicates easily, keeps a good overview and enjoys organising and getting things done. You enjoy working with people from different nationalities and are comfortable picking up the phone and taking initiative.
 A large number of our drivers are Polish and Romanian, so a significant part of the daily communication takes place in English.
